            <ArticleTitle>Analog series-based scaffolds: computational design and exploration of a new type of molecular scaffolds for medicinal chemistry.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>FSO149</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4155/fsoa-2016-0058</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="AIM" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">Computational design of and systematic search for a new type of molecular scaffolds termed analog series-based scaffolds.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="MATERIALS &amp; METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">From currently available bioactive compounds, analog series were systematically extracted, key compounds identified and new scaffolds isolated from them.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Using our computational approach, more than 12,000 scaffolds were extracted from bioactive compounds.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">A new scaffold definition is introduced and a computational methodology developed to systematically identify such scaffolds, yielding a large freely available scaffold knowledge base.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
